WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.757
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:15.913
Unit eleven: Foreign Aid & Development. Today you will say that something holds regardless with -ever clauses.

4
00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:18.877
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:22.938
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:25.469
Development assistance.

7
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:31.351
Development assistance means money or help given to improve a poorer country's economy.

8
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.495
Development assistance paid for new roads.

9
00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:38.409
Your turn. Say: Development assistance.

10
00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.883
Development assistance.

11
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.268
Humanitarian aid.

12
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:52.010
Humanitarian aid means emergency food, medicine and shelter sent to people in crisis.

13
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:55.382
Humanitarian aid reached the village within a day.

14
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:59.147
Your turn. Say: Humanitarian aid.

15
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.698
Humanitarian aid.

16
00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:05.799
Aid dependency.

17
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:11.221
Aid dependency means relying on outside help instead of building local strength.

18
00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:14.141
Aid dependency weakened local farming.

19
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.333
Your turn. Say: Aid dependency.

20
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.737
Aid dependency.

21
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.413
Sustainable development goal.

22
00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:30.528
Sustainable development goal means one of the targets set by the United Nations for a better world.

23
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:34.405
Each sustainable development goal has measurable targets.

24
00:01:35.017 --> 00:01:38.749
Your turn. Say: Sustainable development goal.

25
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.716
Sustainable development goal.

26
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.567
Donor country.

27
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.639
Donor country means a country that gives aid to others.

28
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.842
A donor country pledged ten million dollars.

29
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.172
Your turn. Say: Donor country.

30
00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.278
Donor country.

31
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:02.447
Capacity building.

32
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:08.317
Capacity building means helping people and institutions gain the skills to manage alone.

33
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:11.648
Capacity building trained local engineers.

34
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.949
Your turn. Say: Capacity building.

35
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.335
Capacity building.

36
00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:21.607
Poverty alleviation.

37
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:26.776
Poverty alleviation means reducing the number of people who live in poverty.

38
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:30.358
Poverty alleviation requires jobs as well as aid.

39
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.997
Your turn. Say: Poverty alleviation.

40
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:38.519
Poverty alleviation.

41
00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:40.726
Aid effectiveness.

42
00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:45.214
Aid effectiveness means how well aid achieves lasting results.

43
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:48.908
Aid effectiveness improved when locals led the project.

44
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:52.831
Your turn. Say: Aid effectiveness.

45
00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.039
Aid effectiveness.

46
00:02:57.833 --> 00:03:01.194
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:07.442
Visal, a minister says 'Whatever aid we receive must be spent wisely.' What does 'whatever' mean here?

48
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:20.479
It means 'any aid at all, without limit'. Words with -ever (whatever, whoever, whichever, wherever, whenever, however) introduce clauses that show it makes no difference.

49
00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:23.502
How is it different from 'no matter what'?

50
00:03:24.617 --> 00:03:36.011
'No matter what aid arrives, it must be spent wisely' has the same meaning. 'No matter' is more spoken, while -ever clauses can also act as a subject or an object.

51
00:03:37.117 --> 00:03:39.116
Can you show a subject use?

52
00:03:40.217 --> 00:03:51.033
'Whoever signs the agreement accepts the conditions.' Here 'whoever signs' is the subject. 'Give the grant to whichever district needs it most' shows an object use.

53
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.770
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:59.228
Grammar focus: -ever clauses: whatever and whoever and whichever.

55
00:03:59.528 --> 00:04:00.715
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:04.542
Whatever aid a donor country gives must be spent wisely.

57
00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.274
Whoever signs the agreement accepts the conditions.

58
00:04:09.183 --> 00:04:13.040
No matter how generous the grant is, capacity building takes years.

59
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:22.722
Use whatever, whoever, whichever, wherever, whenever or no matter + wh-word for 'it makes no difference': Whatever aid arrives, spend it wisely.

60
00:04:23.483 --> 00:04:27.320
Be careful! Don't say: Whatever you decide it, we agree.

61
00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:32.543
Say: Whatever you decide, we agree.

62
00:04:32.843 --> 00:04:35.110
Do not repeat the object after whatever.

63
00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.715
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.977
Helping Without Harming.

65
00:04:41.277 --> 00:04:44.658
Development assistance should help countries stand on their own feet.

66
00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:50.174
Whatever form it takes, aid is most effective when local people lead the project.

67
00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:56.974
Whichever sustainable development goal a donor country supports, capacity building must come with the money.

68
00:04:57.967 --> 00:05:03.948
No matter how generous humanitarian aid is, aid dependency can grow if there is no plan to leave.

69
00:05:04.933 --> 00:05:09.580
Whoever designs a programme should measure poverty alleviation, not just spending.

70
00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:15.133
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:19.074
blank wins the election must listen to all citizens.

72
00:05:19.374 --> 00:05:23.248
A, Whoever. B, Whichever. C, Whenever.

73
00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.823
The answer is A: Whoever.

74
00:05:29.983 --> 00:05:33.597
Helping people gain skills to manage for themselves is blank building.

75
00:05:33.897 --> 00:05:37.875
A, capacity. B, donor. C, border.

76
00:05:41.433 --> 00:05:43.503
The answer is A: capacity.

77
00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.522
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:05:46.822 --> 00:05:55.061
A, Whatever you decide, we will support you.. B, Whatever you will decide it, we support you.. C, What you decide ever, we support you..

79
00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.062
The answer is A: Whatever you decide, we will support you..

80
00:06:03.217 --> 00:06:06.250
A country that gives aid to others is a blank country.

81
00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.530
A, host. B, donor. C, member.

82
00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:14.788
The answer is B: donor.

83
00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:19.401
According to the reading, aid works best when who leads the project?

84
00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:24.353
A, foreign experts. B, local people. C, a superpower.

85
00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.981
The answer is B: local people.

86
00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:34.179
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:35.017 --> 00:06:40.000
Can foreign aid sometimes create dependency instead of long-term self-sufficiency?

88
00:06:48.783 --> 00:06:50.249
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:50.549 --> 00:07:18.305
Yes, foreign aid can create dependency if it replaces local effort instead of supporting it. When a country relies on donor grants for basic services, its own institutions may stay weak. Aid works best when it includes capacity building, trains local workers and has a clear plan to reduce support over time so that the country can stand on its own.

90
00:07:18.605 --> 00:07:20.349
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:27.083
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and -ever clauses: whatever and whoever and whichever.

92
00:07:27.383 --> 00:07:33.101
Today's value is social impact. Use your skills and ideas to improve other people's lives.

93
00:07:33.401 --> 00:07:35.984
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:07:36.284 --> 00:07:38.843
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

